A problem may be that a request to a node without a server may be black-holed, i.e. no reject either icmp or http.

Based on this comment the addition of the delete directive definitely seems intentional which makes me lean toward fixing the merge code.
>	// The patch is the difference from current to modified without deletions, plus deletions
	// from original to modified. To find it, we compute deletions, which are the deletions from
	// original to modified, and delta, which is the difference from current to modified without
	// deletions, and then apply delta to deletions as a patch, which should be strictly additive.
	
https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/strategicpatch/patch.go#L2070-L2077

@gnufied, dangling attach does not help here. The volume is still attached to the old node even after ~10 minutes.

